      "result_summary": "DSC confirmed glass transition temperatures of synthesized polyureas, no melting endotherms observed confirming amorphous nature",
      "derived_property_ids": [],
      "evidence": [
        {
          "block_id": "P_1_21",
          "page": 1,
          "bbox": [
            53.0,
            330.0,
            467.0,
            787.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "Differential scanning calorimetry (DSC) and thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) were recorded duplicate on a Stanton Redcraft STA-780 (London, UK) in air at a heating rate of 108C/min. In DSC thermograms, the samples were heated from 30 to $2 0 0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C } ,$ they were cooled, and then re-heated to eliminate the thermal history."
        },
        {
          "block_id": "P_6_84",
          "page": 6,
          "bbox": [
            87.0,
            249.0,
            500.0,
            476.0
          ],
          "source_type": "text",
          "source_sentence": "Also DSC analysis confirmed data obtained from DMTA. The glass transition temperature $( T _ { \\mathrm { g } } )$ was taken as the midpoint of the change in the slope of the baseline. Also, no polymer showed a clear melting endotherm which resulted from the amorphous nature of the polymers."
        }
      ],
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
    },
